## Stripe Webhook

- `POST /v1/billing/webhook` reads `await request.body()` as raw bytes before anything parses it and verifies with `stripe.Webhook.construct_event(...)`; a missing signature or secret answers 400 `BILLING_WEBHOOK_MISCONFIGURED`, a failed verification 400 `BILLING_WEBHOOK_INVALID_SIGNATURE`. Only allowlisted event types are handled, the rest get 200; the route is exempt from CSRF and rate limiting and has no session dependency
- The ledger `billing_webhook_events` (R-334; `stripe_event_id` unique, `status` in `claimed`/`processed`/`failed`, `attempted_at`) makes delivery idempotent: claim with `INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (stripe_event_id) DO UPDATE SET status = 'claimed', attempted_at = now() WHERE status = 'failed' OR (status = 'claimed' AND attempted_at < now() - interval '10 minutes') RETURNING id`, skip when no row returns, and mark `processed` or `failed` in the same transaction as the side effect. `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` never reclaims a `failed` event or a crashed claim, so Stripe's redelivery would be skipped and the event lost
- A failed handler answers 500 `BILLING_WEBHOOK_PROCESSING_FAILED` so Stripe retries

