## Testing (pytest)

- Assert returned values and stored rows, never mock-call counts (R-401); a failing test is fixed or deleted, never skipped
- Integration tests use a real Postgres (compose locally, a service container in CI): schema built once per session with `alembic upgrade head`, each test in a transaction that rolls back (or truncating the touched tables when a test commits)
- API tests drive the app through `httpx.AsyncClient(transport=ASGITransport(app=create_app()))`; `pytest-asyncio` in `asyncio_mode = "auto"`; tests mirror `app/` under `tests/unit` and `tests/integration` (R-313)
- Each input handler has one negative-input test (R-406) asserting the envelope code; provider clients are replaced at the client boundary with recorded responses, and an LLM consumer has one fixture test against a real captured response
- Coverage floor 60 percent on `app/`
- Runs (R-509): `pytest -n auto` (`pytest-xdist`), `--dist loadfile` when a file shares an expensive fixture, one database per worker named from the `worker_id` fixture; turn ends and commits run only the affected tests, and the full suite is the required CI check before merge to `main`; either plugin is a new dependency needing its R-331 justification

---

## Tooling

- **ruff** is the one linter and, through `ruff format`, the formatter for every new repo (`line-length = 100`, matching the portfolio Prettier width); an existing repo keeps the formatter it already configures (black or ruff format), and a repo never runs both. **mypy --strict** runs over `app/` and `tests/`
- Ruff `select` includes `E`, `F`, `I`, `B`, `UP`, `S`, `D`, `ANN`, `PL`; all tool configuration lives in `pyproject.toml`
- Pre-commit runs lint, format, and type check on staged files only; the full sweep runs at pre-push and in CI (R-509); do not re-run what the hooks ran

---

## Enforcement

- `hook:push-ruff-gate` runs `~/.claude/enforce/ruff-enforce.toml` (codes listed in its header; repos in `enforce/exempt-repos.txt` skip it; fails open without ruff or uv) over the added lines of the outgoing diff on `git push`, and `~/.claude/enforce/data-access/python_data_access.py` over the changed files: R-361, a repository- or `db`-imported call or an `execute`/`scalar(s)`/`stream` call inside a loop or comprehension; R-362, inside a `begin()`/`begin_nested()` block, an `httpx`/`requests`/`aiohttp` or `clients` call, or a data-access call not given the transaction's connection. A deliberately bounded loop carries `# data-access-allow: <the bound>`. `D100` and `D103` (R-320) join when `.enforce.json` sets `fileHeaders: true`
- `ci:llm-rule-judge` judges `*.py` against R-316, R-317, R-325, R-334
- `hook:structure-gate` allows `snake_case` package directories plus `db/`, `core/`, `middleware/`, `dependencies/` and denies catch-all directories, kebab-case, and co-located tests; `hook:migration-defaults-guard` checks the Alembic default forms in Migrations

