## Build/Run Assets (R-407)

Python ships source, not a bundle. Runtime-loaded non-code assets (SQL files, prompt markdown in `prompts/`, JSON fixtures the app reads) ship as package data declared in `pyproject.toml`. A smoke test asserts each required asset resolves through `importlib.resources.files("app")`, and the image build runs that test in the builder stage, so a missing asset fails the build rather than the first request. The package contains no `.env*` file and no secret.
